<title>RUSSIA: Russia non-CIS oil exports may rise 25 pct in 3-5.</title>
<headline>Russia non-CIS oil exports may rise 25 pct in 3-5.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's annual crude oil exports outside the Commonwealth of Independent States could rise by up to one quarter to 2.5 million barrels per day in the next three to five years, the Fuel and Energy Ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry, in a comment in its InfoTEK bulletin, said new export terminals could increase delivery potential in the near term. Russian 1996 non-CIS oil exports were 2.0 million bpd.</p>
</text>
